README.md quotes a few short passages from dated public reports: posts on Reddit (r/alexa) and one review
in The Verge. Those passages belong to their authors and publishers. They are quoted briefly, each with
its date and a link to its source, to show the problem Fixwright works on in the words of the people who
had it. This repository does not ship copies of the posts or the review, only the short quotes. If you
wrote one of the quoted posts and want your words taken out, open an issue and the quote will be replaced
with a link alone. The demo video and its script (video/script.txt) quote none of them.

Fonts

apps/host/src/fonts holds Atkinson Hyperlegible Next and Atkinson Hyperlegible Mono by the Braille
Institute, from the @fontsource packages. They are licensed under the SIL Open Font License 1.1, whose
text sits beside the font files (OFL-AtkinsonHyperlegibleNext.txt, OFL-AtkinsonHyperlegibleMono.txt).

homefault

packages/homefault is a git submodule pointing at the separate homefault repository. It carries its own
LICENSE and its own NOTICE for the quotes in its incident scenarios.

